    <!-- Battery -->
    <string name="battery_title">Battery settings</string>
    <string name="battery_body">Your phone may stop Call Timer in the background, so calls might not be cut on time. Allow Call Timer to run without battery limits.</string>
    <string name="battery_saver_off">Battery saver is off</string>
    <string name="battery_unrestricted">No battery limits for Call Timer</string>
    <string name="battery_hint_xiaomi">On Xiaomi, Redmi and Poco phones: turn on Autostart for Call Timer and set Battery saver to \"No restrictions\".</string>
    <string name="battery_hint_samsung">On Samsung phones: open Battery, then set Call Timer to \"Unrestricted\" and remove it from Sleeping apps.</string>
    <string name="battery_hint_oppo">On Oppo, Realme and OnePlus phones: allow Auto launch and turn off battery optimisation for Call Timer.</string>
    <string name="battery_hint_vivo">On Vivo and iQOO phones: allow Background running and Auto-start for Call Timer.</string>

    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="onb1_title">Keep calls short</string>
    <string name="onb1_body">Call Timer puts a time limit on calls, for each phone number:</string>
    <string name="onb1_point1">First call of the day: ends after 10 minutes.</string>
    <string name="onb1_point2">Second call: ends after 5 minutes.</string>
    <string name="onb1_point3">More calls that day are rejected until midnight. Emergency numbers and people you choose are never limited.</string>
    <string name="onb2_title">Keep your phone app</string>
    <string name="onb2_body">Make and answer calls with your normal phone app. Call Timer works quietly in the background. It needs these call permissions:</string>
    <string name="onb2_point_state">See when a call rings, starts and ends.</string>
    <string name="onb2_point_number">See who is calling (call log), so limits are counted per person.</string>
    <string name="onb2_point_end">End a call when the time is up, and reject a caller who used up today\'s calls.</string>
    <string name="onb2_restricted_hint">If Android says \"Restricted setting\": open App settings, tap ⋮ (top right), choose \"Allow restricted settings\", then come back and tap Fix again.</string>
    <string name="onb2_screening_body">Optional: with call screening, numbers that are NOT saved in your contacts are blocked before your phone even rings. Saved contacts are rejected by Call Timer right when they start ringing.</string>
    <string name="onb3_title">Names and calls</string>
    <string name="onb3_contacts_body">Contacts: so you see \"Ravi\" instead of a number, and can pick always-allowed people.</string>
    <string name="onb4_title">Alerts</string>
    <string name="onb4_body">Notifications: to show the time left, warnings, and when a call is ended by the limit.</string>
    <string name="onb4_overlay_body">Show timer over calls: a small \"07:42 left\" pill floats on top of your phone app\'s call screen. You can drag it up or down.</string>
    <string name="onb4_battery_body">Some phones stop apps to save battery. Allow Call Timer to run without battery limits so the timer is always on time.</string>
